caption: Hive Storage
tags: $:/tags/ControlPanel/SettingsTab

! Disable

You can disable the hive storage plugin:

<$checkbox tiddler="$:/config/HiveStorage/Enabled" field="text" checked="yes" unchecked="no" default="yes"> Use indexed database storage</$checkbox>

! Clear

Click this button to clear the indexed database and disable its use:

<$button message="tm-clear-hive-storage">Clear indexed database</$button>

! Save Filter

This filter determines which tiddlers will be saved to the indexed database.

* `[prefix[$:/state/]] -[prefix[$:/state/popup/]]` - the default value. Save state tiddlers except popup state tiddlers, thus preserving selected tabs and the open/closed status of table of contents entries. Any other tiddlers created or changed will be lost after reloading the page.
* `[all[]]` - attempt to save all changed tiddlers. This means even popup state tiddlers and temporary tiddlers will be saved.
* `[all[]] -[prefix[$:/state/popup/]] -[prefix[$:/temp/]] -[prefix[$:/HistoryList]]` - save all tiddlers except popup state tiddlers, temp tiddlers and the history list.

|tc-table-no-border|k
|<$link to="$:/config/HiveStorage/SaveFilter">Hive Storage Save Filter</$link> |<$edit-text tiddler="$:/config/HiveStorage/SaveFilter" default="" tag="input"/> |

! Custom Quota Exceeded Alert

This setting allows a custom alert message to be displayed when an attempt is made to store a tiddler in the indexed database and it fails.

|tc-table-no-border|k
|<$link to="$:/config/HiveStorage/QuotaExceededAlert">Hive Storage Quota Exceeded Alert</$link> |<$edit-text tiddler="$:/config/HiveStorage/QuotaExceededAlert" default="" tag="input"/> |

! Prevent browser from evicting the indexed database

Permission for indexed database persistence: ''{{$:/state/hive/storage/persisted}}''

The first time a tiddler is saved to the indexed database a request will be made to prevent automatic eviction of the database for this site. This means the data will not be cleared unless the user manually clears it.

Old browsers may not support this feature. New browsers might not support the feature if the wiki is hosted on a non-localhost unencrypted http connection.

Some browsers will explicitly prompt the user for permission. Other browsers may automatically grant or deny the request based on site usage or based on whether the site is bookmarked.

! Startup Log

The tiddler $:/temp/HiveStorage/Log contains a log of the tiddlers that were loaded from the indexed database at startup:

